Hi, it's Paula from Italy.
嗨，我是来自意大利的宝拉。

00:00:57.340 --> 00:01:04.099
The first time I watched Elmate Armada was during the first wave of COVID that came March of 2020.
我第一次观看 Elmate Armada 是在 2020 年 3 月爆发的第一波新冠疫情期间。

00:01:04.099 --> 00:01:04.939
My name's Josh.
我叫乔什。

00:01:04.939 --> 00:01:07.500
I first watched the show as a college student in New York.
我第一次看这个节目时还是纽约的一名大学生。

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.579
My name is Anna.
我叫安娜。

00:01:08.579 --> 00:01:11.319
I am in Los Angeles, planet Earth.
我在地球洛杉矶。

00:01:11.319 --> 00:01:19.780
How I met your mother is special because whether I've had a fantastic day or a fucking terrible day, watching that show is always the right move for the mood.
我遇见你母亲的方式很特别，因为无论我度过了美好的一天还是糟糕透顶的一天，观看那个节目总是适合心情的举动。

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:24.040
My friend told me to watch the show and just said, I'm Ted Mosby.
我的朋友让我看这个节目并只是说，我是特德·莫斯比。

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:25.459
I had no idea what he's talking about.
我不知道他在说什么。

00:01:25.459 --> 00:01:30.099
And I watched him and I came back to him when I said, mm-hmm, can't tell mostly.
我看着他，当我说，嗯，嗯，大部分都说不出来时，我又回到了他身边。

00:01:30.099 --> 00:01:34.620
You remember, it was hard time with strict lockdowns and isolation.
你记得，那是一段严格封锁和隔离的艰难时期。

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:43.700
After a very tough day, every night I watched some of my episodes to, let's say, overcome such difficult times.
在经历了非常艰难的一天之后，每天晚上我都会观看一些剧集，以克服这样的困难时期。

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:52.780
It feels right, regardless, to go spend time with those characters, those candid, stumbling, hilarious, raunchy, relentlessly themselves people.
不管怎样，花时间和这些角色在一起感觉是对的，那些坦率、跌跌撞撞、热闹、不修边幅、无情的他们自己。

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:57.219
And that gives the same feeling, the same quality of what good friendship is.
这与良好的友谊有着同样的感觉和品质。

00:01:57.219 --> 00:02:05.060
And being between junior and senior year of college, I was terrified of what was coming next and how to make it happen the way I want.
在大学三年级和四年级之间，我对接下来发生的事情以及如何让它按照我想要的方式发生感到恐惧。

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:07.099
Then there was this wonderful show.
然后就有了这场精彩的表演。

00:02:07.099 --> 00:02:16.590
That was all about how the randomness of life is what gets you exactly where you need to be.
这就是关于生活的随机性如何让你准确地到达你需要的地方。

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:29.000
I'm a lobby soon in New York City when I see you.
当我见到你时，我很快就到了纽约市的大厅。

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:36.879
Please permit me to tell you everything in New York City.
请允许我告诉你纽约市的一切。

00:02:36.879 --> 00:02:39.280
Well, hello, hello.
嗯，你好，你好。

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:41.360
This is Josh Radner.
这是乔什·拉德纳。

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:43.960
I am here with my friend Craig Thomas.
我和我的朋友克雷格·托马斯在这里。

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:45.280
Hi, Josh.
嗨，乔什。

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:46.719
Hey, it's great to be here with you.
嘿，很高兴和你在一起。

00:02:46.719 --> 00:02:50.879
Welcome to the first episode of How We Made Your Mother.
欢迎收看《我们如何成就了你的母亲》第一集。

00:02:50.879 --> 00:02:52.599
Are we calling it Hwimium?
我们称之为 Hwimium 吗？

00:02:52.599 --> 00:02:53.759
I was wondering about that.
我对此感到好奇。

00:02:53.759 --> 00:02:54.599
Hwimium.
Hwimium。

00:02:54.599 --> 00:02:55.639
I think it's Hwimium.
我认为是 Hwimium。

00:02:55.639 --> 00:02:56.599
Does it work?
有效吗？

00:02:56.599 --> 00:02:59.280
I think it does, yeah.
我想确实如此，是的。

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:08.599
So, how I make your mother, which is the show under discussion, is a show that ran on CBS from 2005 to 2014.
那么，我们正在讨论的节目《我如何塑造你的母亲》是哥伦比亚广播公司 (CBS) 2005 年至 2014 年播出的一档节目。

00:03:08.599 --> 00:03:09.520
Is that right, Craig?
是这样吗，克雷格？

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:11.240
That is correct, nine seasons.
没错，九季。

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:12.080
Nine seasons.
九个季节。

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:16.840
So, almost a decade of our lives, I played the eye in how I made your mother.
所以，在我们生命的近十年里，我一直在扮演如何塑造你母亲的角色。

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:23.680
I played the character of Ted Mosby for nine seasons and Craig tell us what you did on the show.
我扮演了泰德·莫斯比这个角色九季，克雷格告诉我们你在剧中做了什么。

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:25.599
I was Barney.
我是巴尼。

00:03:25.599 --> 00:03:27.719
No, that's right, I remember that.
不，是这样，我记得。

00:03:27.719 --> 00:03:32.800
I have not aged well, if you're watching on the YouTube.
如果你在 YouTube 上观看的话，我还没有老好。

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:41.479
No, I'm the co-creator of the show, along with my very brilliant writing partner, Carter Bays, who will be a guest on here to discuss future and future episodes.
不，我是该剧的共同创作者，还有我非常出色的编剧搭档卡特·贝斯（Carter Bays），他将作为嘉宾来讨论未来和未来的剧集。

00:03:41.479 --> 00:03:47.039
And we were lucky enough to create the show that found our way to the likes of you, Mr. Ratner.
拉特纳先生，我们很幸运能够制作出这样的节目，并受到了像您这样的人的喜爱。

00:03:47.039 --> 00:03:47.879
Oh, thanks.
哦，谢谢。

00:03:47.879 --> 00:03:53.639
Well, Craig and I have obviously been friends now for coming on two decades, which is astonishing.
嗯，克雷格和我显然已经是二十年来的朋友了，这令人惊讶。

00:03:53.639 --> 00:03:55.439
We both now live in New York.
我们现在都住在纽约。

00:03:55.439 --> 00:04:07.639
About once a year, I would say, we have a habit of grabbing a meal or some drinks and talk inevitably turns to how I made your mother as well as other things that are happening in our lives.
我想说，大约每年一次，我们都有吃一顿饭或喝点饮料的习惯，谈话不可避免地会转向我如何创造你的母亲以及我们生活中发生的其他事情。

00:04:07.639 --> 00:04:18.120
But I so enjoy talking about how I made your mother with you and unpacking this thing we made that has been the biggest gift and has carried a lot of shadow with it.
但我非常喜欢谈论我如何与你一起创造你的母亲，并打开我们制作的这个东西的包装，它是最大的礼物，并带有很多阴影。

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:24.759
And it's just like all things is a very complicated thing, but also a very beautiful thing.
就像所有的事物都是一件非常复杂的事情，但同时也是一件非常美丽的事情一样。

00:04:24.759 --> 00:04:28.680
And you're the person I love talking about this show with the most.
你是我最喜欢谈论这个节目的人。

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:31.480
So when this idea struck me like, you know what?
所以当我想到这个想法时，你知道吗？

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:38.800
It's actually time for me to turn around and revisit how I met your mother, but also watch it a lot of the episodes for the first time.
事实上，我是时候回过头来回顾一下我是如何认识你母亲的，而且很多情节都是第一次看。

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:41.079
I only watched about half the episodes, what it was on.
我只看了大约一半的剧集，内容是什么。

00:04:41.079 --> 00:04:48.959
So I will be rewatching the show along with you and our listeners, some of whom I assume will be coming to the show for the first time.
因此，我将与您和我们的听众一起重新观看该节目，我认为其中一些人将是第一次观看该节目。

00:04:48.959 --> 00:04:54.199
Other ones will have watched it many times and are just looking for the backstage notes here.
其他人可能已经看过很多次了，只是在这里寻找后台笔记。

00:04:54.199 --> 00:05:06.167
But I figured if I'm going to do this, why don't we, why don't we put it on the record and actually just walk through the show together and much like the older wiser narrator Ted, which we are now around that age.
但我想，如果我要这样做，我们为什么不，为什么我们不把它记录下来，实际上只是一起走过这个节目，就像年长的、更明智的叙述者泰德一样，我们现在大约在那个年龄。

00:05:06.167 --> 00:05:10.156
Let's look back and see who we were, who we are now, where we're going.
让我们回顾一下，看看我们曾经是谁，现在是谁，我们要去哪里。

00:05:10.156 --> 00:05:13.639
And yeah, what else would you say about what we're doing here?
是的，对于我们在这里所做的事情，您还有什么想说的吗？

00:05:13.639 --> 00:05:16.348
Well, first of all, I can't believe you only watched half of the episodes.
好吧，首先，我不敢相信你只看了一半的剧集。

00:05:16.348 --> 00:05:17.079
I'm deeply offended.
我深感被冒犯。

00:05:17.079 --> 00:05:18.457
I think I'm just going to walk off.
我想我要走开。

00:05:18.457 --> 00:05:19.560
I'm walking off the project.
我要离开这个项目了。

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:26.680
No, the truth is, I haven't rewatched the show door-to-door since it went off.
不，事实是，自从节目播出以来，我还没有挨家挨户地重看过。

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:29.319
I've seen episodes, but I haven't watched a door-to-door.
我看过几集，但没看过挨家挨户的。

00:05:29.319 --> 00:05:33.360
And so I think what we're doing here is excavating back into our past.
所以我认为我们在这里所做的就是挖掘我们的过去。

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:36.040
It was almost a decade of our lives.
这几乎是我们生命中的十年。

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:39.160
And we're trying to figure out what did we do there?
我们试图弄清楚我们在那里做了什么？

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:40.160
What happened?
发生了什么？

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:41.160
What happened?
发生了什么？

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:42.160
We made this thing.
我们做了这个东西。

00:05:42.160 --> 00:05:43.160
It's like the pineapple episode.
这就像菠萝情节。

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:44.160
You're like, what?
你就像，什么？

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:45.160
We have to piece it together.
我们必须把它拼凑起来。

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:49.439
We're doing the pineapple incident, but for the entire series, what happened?
我们正在做菠萝事件，但是对于整个系列来说，发生了什么？

00:05:49.439 --> 00:05:56.199
We woke up, we woke up, we're we've awakened and we're almost 50 or I think you're a bureaucrat there and I'm almost there.
我们醒了，我们醒了，我们已经醒了，我们已经快50岁了，或者我认为你是那里的官僚，而我也快到了。

00:05:56.199 --> 00:05:59.860
And we're kind of going, wait, we are closer to the age of future Ted.
我们正在走，等等，我们离未来特德的时代更近了。

00:05:59.860 --> 00:06:05.459
We are closer to 2030 and then we were to do that, we are to 2005 when the show launched.
我们已经接近 2030 年，然后我们就可以做到这一点，我们已经到了 2005 年该节目推出的时候。

00:06:05.459 --> 00:06:06.720
And it is just it is strange.
只是很奇怪。

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:09.120
I was thinking about the sort of symmetry of it.
我在思考它的对称性。

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:16.079
We are something like I think 20 years since the premiere, I think this September will be 20 years since the premiere.
我们就像是首映二十周年，我想今年九月首映二十周年了。

00:06:16.079 --> 00:06:21.600
We are just past 10 years of it, of the finale airing, of it finishing airing.
我们已经过去十年了，它的结局播出，它的结束播出。

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:25.800
So there's a lot of round numbers, there's a 20 and there's a 10 and here we are.
所以有很多整数，有 20，有 10，我们在这里。

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:29.800
And it just seems like a good moment to kind of look back and take stock of it.
这似乎是回顾和评估它的好时机。

00:06:29.800 --> 00:06:30.800
Yeah.
是的。

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:40.439
I, another thing that I, when I called you to talk about this that I really wanted to talk about, I said, I am a astonished one at the kind of long tail of the show.
我，另一件事，当我打电话给你谈论这个我真正想谈论的事情时，我说，我对这部剧的长尾感到惊讶。

00:06:40.439 --> 00:06:52.430
You know, a lot of shows go off the air and, and they go off the air, they go away, you know, and maybe they come up randomly in a, I don't know, trivia night or, you know, remember that, a moment will come back to you.
你知道，很多节目都停播了，然后它们停播了，它们就消失了，你知道，也许它们会在一个我不知道的琐事之夜中随机出现，或者，你知道，记住这一点，一会儿你就会回想起。

00:06:52.430 --> 00:07:04.139
But there's something about how I made my mother one, it keeps minting new fans, so people that were babies, children, or even in their teens when it was on have now discovered it.
但我是如何让我的母亲成为这样的人的，它不断地吸引着新的粉丝，所以当它播出时，婴儿、儿童甚至十几岁的人现在都发现了它。

00:07:04.139 --> 00:07:05.899
I also think there's a really sweet thing.
我也觉得有一个非常甜蜜的事情。

00:07:05.899 --> 00:07:08.339
I think parents are showing it to their teenage kids now.
我认为父母现在正在向十几岁的孩子展示它。

00:07:08.339 --> 00:07:16.006
They're like, this show taught me a lot about, you know, being an adult or a young adult navigating all these things.
他们就像，这个节目教会了我很多关于，你知道，作为一个成年人或一个年轻人如何应对所有这些事情。

00:07:16.006 --> 00:07:19.085
But also, I'm astonished at a number of things.
但同时，我对很多事情感到惊讶。

00:07:19.085 --> 00:07:28.717
But one of the ones that strikes me about when I hear from how I made my mother fan, something I hear so consistently that it's not just anecdotal.
但当我听到我如何让我母亲成为粉丝时，令我印象深刻的是，我经常听到这样的事情，这不仅仅是轶事。

00:07:28.717 --> 00:07:45.360
There has to be something there, which is that people say, I got turned on to the show or I started watching the show when I was in a really hard moment of my life, whether it's, you know, it's going through a divorce or a sickness or my parent had died.
那里一定有一些东西，那就是人们说，我开始看这个节目，或者当我处于人生中非常困难的时刻时，我开始看这个节目，无论是，你知道，正在经历离婚、生病还是我的父母去世。

00:07:47.439 --> 00:07:50.385
I was having a personal kind of moment of crisis.
我正经历着个人的危机时刻。

00:07:50.385 --> 00:07:58.560
And there seems to be that this thing I've noticed that how I met your mother is like soul medicine for people going through hard times.
我注意到，我是如何认识你母亲的，这件事似乎对于经历困难时期的人来说就像是灵魂良药。

00:07:59.360 --> 00:08:02.709
And I don't know that it was conceived of that exactly.
我不知道它是否是这样构想的。

00:08:02.709 --> 00:08:07.338
I don't think you and Carter sat out in 2004 and said, I know what we'll do.
我不认为你和卡特在 2004 年袖手旁观并说，我知道我们会做什么。

00:08:07.338 --> 00:08:09.470
We'll do a sole panacea for people.
我们将为人们做唯一的灵丹妙药。

00:08:09.470 --> 00:08:12.454
But it seems like that's what it does for people.
但这似乎就是它对人们的作用。

00:08:12.454 --> 00:08:17.205
And I hear it so consistently that it strikes me as something worth exploring.
我经常听到它，这让我觉得它是值得探索的东西。

00:08:17.205 --> 00:08:18.362
It's such an honor.
真是太荣幸了。

00:08:18.362 --> 00:08:24.818
People come up to us all the time and to you Josh and say the show got them through something really hard.
人们总是来找我们和乔什，说这部剧帮助他们度过了非常艰难的时期。

00:08:24.818 --> 00:08:30.970
And getting that, or they say, I married my wife because we realized we're both how much mother fans.
明白了这一点，或者他们说，我嫁给了我的妻子，因为我们意识到我们都是妈妈的粉丝。

00:08:30.970 --> 00:08:33.223
So they met in an event or something.
所以他们是在一次活动或者什么事情上认识的。

00:08:33.223 --> 00:08:39.679
It's just just the ways the show has been crucial in people's lives, like the opening words from the fans.
这只是这部剧对人们生活至关重要的方式，就像粉丝们的开场白一样。

00:08:39.679 --> 00:08:41.600
We have the greatest fans of any fans.
我们拥有所有粉丝中最伟大的粉丝。

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:43.519
How much more the fans are so amazing.
何况粉丝们还这么厉害。

00:08:43.519 --> 00:08:44.519
Huge shout out to the fans.
向粉丝们大声喊叫。

00:08:44.519 --> 00:08:47.159
If you were listening to this, you were an amazing person.
如果你听到这个，你就是一个了不起的人。

00:08:47.159 --> 00:08:52.840
And I find such an openness, Josh, to come talk to us about stuff.
乔什，我发现自己很愿意来和我们谈论一些事情。

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:54.919
Do you get this a little bit?
你明白一点了吗？

00:08:54.919 --> 00:09:01.360
Cause I'm a writer and people I have to go around telling people I wear a little shirt that says I create a how much mother and just you got that needy.
因为我是一名作家，我必须到处告诉人们我穿着一件小衬衫，上面写着我创造了一个多少母亲，而你有那么需要。

00:09:01.360 --> 00:09:03.879
I wear it on my face, I have a tattooed on my face.
我把它戴在脸上，我的脸上有纹身。

00:09:03.879 --> 00:09:05.799
You have tattooed on your face.
你的脸上有纹身。

00:09:05.799 --> 00:09:10.679
And I've been dying for years to ask you the sort of two-part question.
