泰德是一个复杂的角色。

00:18:25.420 --> 00:18:29.547
He's a complicated character to have played because he's the eyes and ears.
他是一个复杂的角色，因为他是眼睛和耳朵。

00:18:29.547 --> 00:18:31.088
He's the center of the show.
他是整场演出的中心人物。

00:18:31.088 --> 00:18:34.059
He's the person that kind of welcomes the audience in.
他是那种欢迎观众进来的人。

00:18:34.059 --> 00:18:38.679
But he was also his own really flawed, dimensional character.
但他也是他自己真正有缺陷的、立体的性格。

00:18:38.679 --> 00:18:44.813
And I have found the people who relate to Ted are unbelievably fascinating to me.
我发现与特德有联系的人对我来说令人难以置信的着迷。

00:18:44.813 --> 00:18:49.508
Just as many women come up to me and say, I'm like Ted as men.
正如许多女性走过来对我说，作为男人，我就像特德一样。

00:18:49.508 --> 00:18:50.720
Oh, I love that.
哦，我喜欢那个。

00:18:50.720 --> 00:18:52.765
Which is really incredible.
这真是令人难以置信。

00:18:52.765 --> 00:18:53.265
Yeah.
是的。

00:18:53.265 --> 00:18:58.187
But just like people who are worried they feel a little too much.
但就像担心的人一样，他们感觉有点太多了。

00:18:58.187 --> 00:19:03.261
You know, Ted was probably a HSP is that a highly sensitive person.
要知道，Ted 可能是一个 HSP，是一个高度敏感的人。

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:05.929
I think that's fair to say.
我认为这样说是公平的。

00:19:05.929 --> 00:19:15.508
You know, and he just had a big heart and it sometimes got in the way of social, you know, what was expected of him.
你知道，他只是有一颗宽广的心，有时这会妨碍社交，你知道，人们对他的期望。

00:19:15.508 --> 00:19:22.362
But I just, you know, it's an honor to have played someone that kind of raw, right?
但我只是，你知道，能扮演那种原始的人是我的荣幸，对吧？

00:19:22.362 --> 00:19:25.334
Whose nerve endings were so exposed.
谁的神经末梢如此暴露。

00:19:25.334 --> 00:19:30.619
And it helped me, you know, it helped me become more vulnerable.
它帮助了我，你知道，它帮助我变得更加脆弱。

00:19:30.619 --> 00:19:40.446
Disclose parts of myself that maybe I was embarrassed about that you guys were demanding that they be front and center.
透露一下我自己的部分，也许我对你们要求他们站在前面和中心感到尴尬。

00:19:40.446 --> 00:19:46.391
And to also be even at that time, 2005 to be a publicly vulnerable male.
甚至在2005年的那个时候，也是一个公开的弱势男性。

00:19:46.391 --> 00:19:48.373
It's still caring risks.
仍需关注风险。

00:19:48.373 --> 00:19:49.859
How about now too?
现在也怎么样？

00:19:49.859 --> 00:19:52.299
I mean, it carries risks.
我的意思是，它带有风险。

00:19:52.299 --> 00:19:59.539
But it was like a big grave thing you guys asked of me and I'm grateful and I'm glad that it resonates with people and continues to.
但这就像你们向我提出的一件大事，我很感激，我很高兴它能引起人们的共鸣，并继续下去。

00:19:59.539 --> 00:20:03.339
And it's funny what you said about being vulnerable because it was vulnerable to right too.
你所说的脆弱性很有趣，因为它也容易受到权利的影响。

00:20:03.339 --> 00:20:08.779
Carder and I are these like super emo, like sort of we are highly sensitive people.
卡德和我都是超级情绪化的人，就像我们是高度敏感的人一样。

00:20:08.779 --> 00:20:10.420
We wear our hearts on our sleeves.
我们把我们的心挂在袖子上。

00:20:10.420 --> 00:20:12.740
We have big dreams like Ted.
我们像特德一样有远大的梦想。

00:20:12.740 --> 00:20:18.460
The creation of the show, when we were 30 years old, that was a far-fetched impossible dream to create the show.
节目的创作，在我们30岁的时候，创作节目那是一个遥不可及的不可能的梦想。

00:20:18.460 --> 00:20:24.420
that was us Ted Moes being all over the place, coming up with some big, far-fetched plan that should never have worked out at rain.
那是我们特德·莫斯到处乱跑，想出了一些宏大的、牵强的计划，而这些计划在雨天根本不应该实现。

00:20:24.420 --> 00:20:31.819
But somehow it did demanding that it rain and somehow it worked out of not in all the ways we thought it would, which is the same story for Ted.
但不知何故，它确实要求下雨，而且不知何故，结果并不像我们想象的那样，这对特德来说也是同样的故事。

00:20:31.819 --> 00:20:38.900
It never goes exactly how you plan, but it becomes beautiful in some different way than you ever could have imagined that was the show.
它永远不会完全按照你的计划进行，但它会以某种不同于你想象的方式变得美丽。

00:20:38.900 --> 00:20:45.420
What's funny is, Cardinier very much liked that Marshall's a really sweet, emotional, open-hearted warm softy of a guy.
有趣的是，卡迪尼尔非常喜欢马歇尔，他是一个非常可爱、情绪化、心胸开阔、温暖而温柔的人。

00:20:45.420 --> 00:20:53.420
He's basically had one, you know, girlfriend became this wife, and we would get these notes early on sometimes from well-meaning executives.
他基本上有一个，你知道，女朋友变成了这位妻子，有时我们会很早就从善意的高管那里得到这些笔记。

00:20:55.099 --> 00:21:03.754
Early, and before the show was launched, probably before we even cast it, but also maybe early in the run, where we get these notes, the characters were so based on us at first, right?
早期，在节目推出之前，可能在我们选角之前，但也可能在运行的早期，我们得到这些笔记，角色一开始就是以我们为基础的，对吧？

00:21:03.754 --> 00:21:06.105
And then it became like creating it with you guys.
然后就变成了和你们一起创造它。

00:21:06.105 --> 00:21:07.564
But at first, it really was us.
但一开始，确实是我们。

00:21:07.564 --> 00:21:09.680
And we would get these notes from executives.
我们会从高管那里得到这些笔记。

00:21:09.680 --> 00:21:13.019
It would be the effect of like, these guys are just such fucking whims.
这会产生这样的效果，这些家伙就是这么他妈的突发奇想。

00:21:13.019 --> 00:21:14.469
That's how it felt.
就是这样的感觉。

00:21:14.469 --> 00:21:23.320
It was just like, we would get notes that to the effect of like, no man would ever, no man would call himself a man.
就像，我们会收到这样的注释，大意是，没有人会，没有人会称自己为男人。

00:21:23.320 --> 00:21:27.135
Self-respecting man would ever behave in this way.
有自尊心的人永远都会这样做。

00:21:27.135 --> 00:21:31.637
We're like, um, well, that's based on something that I did.
我们就像，嗯，嗯，这是基于我所做的事情。

00:21:31.637 --> 00:21:34.078
And it was really, really weird.
这真的非常非常奇怪。

00:21:34.078 --> 00:21:45.599
And I think it was my little glimpse at probably how it felt to you in literally your body, embodying the character, and you had to sort of carry that.
我认为这可能是我对你身体的感受的一点小小的瞥见，体现了这个角色，你必须带着它。

00:21:45.599 --> 00:21:49.880
The MTV show Jackass, you were doing that with your heart on CBS every Monday night.
MTV 节目《Jackass》，每周一晚上你都会在 CBS 上用心做这件事。

00:21:49.880 --> 00:21:55.400
You were just like, what happens if we push Ted's heart off a cliff in a shopping cart?
你就像，如果我们用购物车把特德的心推下悬崖，会发生什么？

00:21:55.400 --> 00:21:56.880
Let's see what happens.
让我们看看会发生什么。

00:21:56.880 --> 00:22:03.720
And it's just like there was kind of a stunt and emotional stuntman quality to that, and you were kind of doing your own stunts.
这就像有一种特技和情感特技演员的品质，而你是在做你自己的特技。

00:22:03.720 --> 00:22:21.829
Yeah, especially when there's so much confusion between, you know, you know, you play a character and especially if it's the first introduction to you, you know, I didn't have a lot of public things, but I mean, I had pilots in series that didn't go anywhere and so this was where people kind of met me.
是的，尤其是当你扮演一个角色之间存在如此多的混乱，特别是如果这是第一次向你介绍时，你知道，我没有太多公开的东西，但我的意思是，我有一系列的试播集，但没有去任何地方，所以这就是人们认识我的地方。

00:22:21.829 --> 00:22:33.921
So they thought, well, this is who this is, you know, I do remember at the beginning of I think second or third season, but I don't remember which one, but no, no, it's the beginning of third season.
所以他们想，好吧，这就是这个人，你知道，我确实记得在第二季或第三季的开头，但我不记得是哪一个，但不，不，这是第三季的开头。

00:22:33.921 --> 00:22:38.599
And you guys wanted to really send Ted and Barney out on a lot of adventures.
你们确实想让泰德和巴尼出去进行很多冒险。

00:22:38.599 --> 00:22:45.975
And you started writing Ted as a little more Barney-ish in terms of like he was open to like one night stands and all this stuff.
你开始把泰德写得有点像巴尼式的，因为他对一夜情和所有这些东西都持开放态度。

00:22:45.975 --> 00:22:53.466
And I remember Pam told me that you guys got a note that said, you know, there's a lot of Barney's on TV, but there's only one Ted.
我记得帕姆告诉我，你们收到一张纸条，上面写着，电视上有很多巴尼的角色，但只有一个特德。

00:22:53.466 --> 00:22:54.666
Let's let's keep him.
我们就留着他吧。

00:22:54.666 --> 00:22:57.240
Let's preserve his Tedness or his Mosby-ness.
让我们保留他的泰德风格或莫斯比风格。

00:22:57.240 --> 00:22:58.129
Yeah, totally.
是的，完全可以。

00:22:58.129 --> 00:23:08.680
And we had a lot of really smart, strong female voices from this video and the network who really got the emotion behind the show and we're kind of guardians of that.
我们从这个视频和网络中得到了很多非常聪明、强有力的女性声音，她们真正理解了节目背后的情感，我们是它的守护者。

00:23:08.680 --> 00:23:10.091
And that doesn't always happen.
但这并不总是发生。

00:23:10.091 --> 00:23:11.229
And that was really nice.
那真是太好了。

00:23:11.229 --> 00:23:14.826
And it's not like that fit in with every other show on the network at the time.
这并不适合当时网络上的所有其他节目。

00:23:14.826 --> 00:23:15.873
And that was preserved.
那被保留下来了。

00:23:15.873 --> 00:23:17.922
And it was what was beautiful about the show.
这就是这场演出的美妙之处。

00:23:17.922 --> 00:23:18.559
And thank God.
感谢上帝。

00:23:18.559 --> 00:23:25.480
I wanted to do a quick little pause and just say, our producer, Alec Lev, our wonderful and heroic producer without whom we wouldn't be doing this show.
我想稍微停顿一下，然后说，我们的制片人，亚历克·列夫，我们出色而英勇的制片人，没有他我们就不会做这个节目。

00:23:25.480 --> 00:23:28.899
Well, chime in from time to time with a question or guidance.
好吧，时不时地提出问题或指导。

00:23:28.899 --> 00:23:31.478
Thank you guys for, for bringing me into this.
谢谢你们，让我参与其中。

00:23:31.478 --> 00:23:34.057
And I'm excited to be on the journey with you.
我很高兴能与您一起踏上旅程。

00:23:34.057 --> 00:23:36.749
And yeah, you might hear some questions from me.
是的，你可能会听到我的一些问题。

00:23:36.749 --> 00:23:40.281
My first one here if I could just throw one in Josh's wine now.
我的第一个在这里，如果我现在可以在乔希的酒里扔一个的话。

00:23:40.281 --> 00:23:43.252
I know you've had 10 years podcasts have been around.
我知道播客已经存在 10 年了。

00:23:43.252 --> 00:23:49.139
You've been thinking about this show and then all of a sudden Craig got the call and then I got the call.
你一直在考虑这个节目，然后突然克雷格接到了电话，然后我也接到了电话。

00:23:49.139 --> 00:23:51.438
You'd like to think about about this now.
你现在想考虑一下这个问题。

00:23:51.438 --> 00:23:53.904
And I'm wondering what you're talking about.
我想知道你在说什么。

00:23:53.904 --> 00:23:59.960
But this answer will include your lovely new wife, because I'm eager to talk about that spark of it all too.
但这个答案将包括你可爱的新妻子，因为我也很想谈论这一切的火花。

00:23:59.960 --> 00:24:05.391
Yeah, well, I did get married a year ago, almost exactly a year ago.
是的，嗯，我确实在一年前结婚了，几乎整整一年前。

00:24:05.391 --> 00:24:06.109
Congrats.
恭喜。

00:24:06.109 --> 00:24:09.554
And you know, I got married at 49.
你知道，我 49 岁就结婚了。

00:24:09.554 --> 00:24:18.569
I mean, I, it took me a while to both meet my wife and to almost be ready to get married.
我的意思是，我花了一段时间才见到我的妻子并几乎准备好结婚。

00:24:18.569 --> 00:24:23.009
And I had, without going too much into it, I had challenges in relationships.
我在人际关系方面也遇到了挑战，尽管没有过多考虑。

00:24:23.009 --> 00:24:25.970
They were never, I found them easy to get into.
他们从来都不是，我发现他们很容易进入。

00:24:25.970 --> 00:24:27.650
I found them hard to sustain.
我发现它们很难维持。

00:24:27.650 --> 00:24:28.849
Let's just say that.
就这么说吧。

00:24:28.849 --> 00:24:46.250
And a lot of that's between me and my therapist, but the journey of kind of becoming the man I, who could stand in front of my wife and make that kind of commitment was quite a journey.
其中很多是我和我的治疗师之间的事情，但是成为一个可以站在我妻子面前并做出这种承诺的男人的旅程是一段相当长的旅程。

00:24:46.250 --> 00:24:51.480
And I felt, you know, and it was different.
我感觉，你知道，这是不同的。

00:24:51.480 --> 00:24:54.640
Like I said, like my challenges and relationships were different.
就像我说的，我的挑战和人际关系是不同的。

00:24:54.640 --> 00:25:02.519
Like I used to joke with people that say, you know, Ted has to be careful not to get married on the first date, but I had to be careful not to get divorced on the first date.
就像我以前和人们开玩笑说，你知道，特德必须小心不要在第一次约会时结婚，但我必须小心不要在第一次约会时离婚。

00:25:02.519 --> 00:25:07.079
I was always like looking for the problem kind of thing, not like falling in love so quickly.
我总是喜欢寻找问题之类的事情，而不喜欢那么快坠入爱河。

00:25:07.079 --> 00:25:23.841
But I think there's something about turning 50, having gotten married and just done some work around some of the shadowy aspects of playing Ted being thought of as a person that you're not, you know, some of that was really hard for me.
但我认为 50 岁了，结婚了，刚刚做了一些工作，解决了扮演 Ted 时被认为是一个你不是的人的一些阴暗方面，你知道，其中一些对我来说真的很难。

00:25:23.841 --> 00:25:28.529
It was really hard to navigate just in the realm of like identity.
仅仅在相似的身份领域中导航真的很困难。

00:25:28.529 --> 00:25:29.523
Like who am I?
比如我是谁？

00:25:29.523 --> 00:25:31.370
Who do I self conceive of?
我自己设想的是谁？

00:25:31.370 --> 00:25:54.879
Who do I think I am versus like all these people are telling me, you know, that's not your name, your name is not Josh, you have to be rolling around New York City with Ted and Varity and you are, but March of the Barney and you are, you know, and it felt like this almost theft of my sense of self, like it was really a challenge.
我认为我是谁，就像所有这些人告诉我的那样，你知道，那不是你的名字，你的名字不是乔什，你必须和泰德和瓦瑞蒂一起在纽约市转悠，而你是，但巴尼的三月和你是，你知道，这感觉就像是我的自我意识几乎被偷走了，就像这真的是一个挑战。

00:25:54.880 --> 00:26:05.323
But as the years have gone by, the people who say, I had a guy from Turkey yesterday, two days ago, stopped me, came running out of coffee shop to stop me.
但随着时间的流逝，人们说，昨天，两天前，我有一个来自土耳其的人阻止了我，从咖啡店跑出来阻止我。

00:26:05.323 --> 00:26:11.724
And he said, um, thank you so much for teaching us to believe in love, to believe in ourselves.
他说，嗯，非常感谢你教会我们相信爱，相信我们自己。

00:26:11.724 --> 00:26:15.969
That's an amazing thing to hear on like a right morning, right?
听到这样的消息真是太棒了，就像一个正确的早晨，对吧？

00:26:15.969 --> 00:26:17.182
11 on the morning.
上午11点。

00:26:17.182 --> 00:26:17.682
Yeah.
是的。

00:26:17.682 --> 00:26:31.023
And Jordan, my wife is really good at making me kind of pinch myself in those moments when she's with me, like to say like, do you see that you You were a part of something that really moved people.
乔丹，我的妻子真的很擅长让我在她和我在一起的那些时刻掐自己，比如，你看到了吗？你是真正感动人们的事情的一部分。

00:26:30.859 --> 00:26:47.170
So the people who, it's outweighed by, you know, any of that shadowy stuff is outweighed by the people who just say like, you know, like Rob Delaney in his book, saying, my wife and I needed to laugh and we watched how I met your mother when our son was sick in the hospital.
所以，那些被那些阴暗的东西所压倒的人，被那些只是说，你知道，就像罗布·德莱尼在他的书中说的那样的人所压倒，他说，我和我的妻子需要笑，当我们的儿子生病住院时，我们看着我是如何见到你母亲的。

00:26:47.170 --> 00:27:07.210
Like, things like that, it's made me, almost in like a, like a Jungian way, like to say, All right, there's part of Ted that is, I wrote pretty extensively about this in my newsletter, but maybe a year or two ago, but about Ted's a part of me.
就像这样的事情，它让我，几乎以一种荣格的方式，想说，好吧，这是泰德的一部分，也就是说，我在时事通讯中写了相当多的内容，但也许是一两年前，但关于泰德是我的一部分。

00:27:07.210 --> 00:27:11.410
He's literally a part I played, but he's not all of me.
他确实是我扮演的一个角色，但他并不是我的全部。

00:27:11.410 --> 00:27:16.569
Yeah, and I think for a long time, I was like trying to be like, that's not me, that's not me.
是的，我想很长一段时间以来，我都在努力表现出，那不是我，那不是我。

00:27:16.569 --> 00:27:22.099
Like I was in rejection of him and I would not take roles that evoked him and I was really fighting him.
就像我在拒绝他一样，我不会扮演那些能唤起他的角色，我真的是在与他作斗争。

00:27:22.099 --> 00:27:35.256
And I think there's something about the time in my life right now maybe it's just literally the mercy of time that has allowed me to say, all right, you know, let's turn around and look at this guy.
我认为现在我生命中的这段时间也许只是时间的仁慈让我能够说，好吧，你知道，让我们转身看看这个家伙。

00:27:35.256 --> 00:27:37.914
Let's look at this character you played.
我们来看看你扮演的这个角色。

00:27:37.914 --> 00:27:41.768
Let's look at who you were when you played this character.
让我们看看你扮演这个角色时是谁。

00:27:41.768 --> 00:27:45.888
And look, I was a different person in 2005 than I was in 2014.
你看，2005 年的我和 2014 年的我是一个不同的人。

00:27:45.888 --> 00:27:49.276
And so are you a big time, you know, a lot, change.
你知道，你也经历了很多变化。

00:27:49.276 --> 00:27:52.400
And I'm a lot different now than I was in 2014.
现在的我与 2014 年相比有很大不同。

00:27:52.400 --> 00:27:52.900
Yeah.
是的。

00:27:52.900 --> 00:28:02.667
So I think it was just, you know, there's something allowed me the space and the grace and the patience with myself to go, let's stop running away.
所以我认为这只是，你知道，有某种东西给了我空间、优雅和对自己的耐心，让我们停止逃跑。

00:28:02.500 --> 00:28:06.299
Let's actually, this is going to be in my obituary.
事实上，这将出现在我的讣告中。

00:28:06.299 --> 00:28:10.259
A lot of people recognize me from it and still want to talk about it.
很多人从中认出了我，并且仍然想谈论它。

